WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.950
President Eisenhower seemed the picture&nbsp;
of health in these films made in Denver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:08.700
just before his sudden heart attack&nbsp;
nearing the end of his work in play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.260
vacation the President appeared rested&nbsp;
refreshed and an unusually good spirits

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.290
stricken at the Lafayette Street home of&nbsp;
mrs. Eisenhower's mother the president was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:24.730
helped into a car in the early morning&nbsp;
hours rushed along the street to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:29.200
Fitzsimmons Army Hospital and placed in&nbsp;
an oxygen tent in an eighth floor suite

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.970
meanwhile leaving Washington for Denso a&nbsp;
press secretary James Haggerty and Colonel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:43.090
Thomas Mattingly a heart specialist from Walter&nbsp;
Reed Army Hospital in the Denver church where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:48.070
he worshiped in churches and synagogues&nbsp;
all across a shocked nation Americans of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:53.560
many faiths and many creeds United in one&nbsp;
prayer a speedy and full recovery for their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:58.180
president though the heart attack was not&nbsp;
severe the fear of complications weighed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:03.820
on the hearts and minds of the people&nbsp;
leading the church goers in Washington&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:09.250
was Vice President Nixon facing grave new&nbsp;
burdens in the fateful days ahead pledging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:15.400
a continuance of Ike's program summoned to the&nbsp;
hospital for an emergency consultation a famed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:20.800
Boston heart specialist dr. Paul Dudley white&nbsp;
declared prospects were reasonably good for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:26.110
president's complete recovery also arriving&nbsp;
was Major John Eisenhower staying in a room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:32.620
across the hall from his father and anxious&nbsp;
vigil as America waited and prayed and hoped

